# Version control
.git
.github

# IDEs, AI agent scratch, and OS junk
.idea/
.vscode/
.gemini/
# See the note in .gcloudignore: .claude/ holds git worktrees, which are full
# repository checkouts and dwarf the real build context.
.claude/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Build and package caches
# Docker ignore patterns are not gitignore patterns: a bare `__pycache__/`
# matches only the context root. Without the `**/` form, a developer who ran
# the skill tests before `make docker-build` ships their bytecode — including
# .pyc files for modules that have since been renamed away.
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
**/*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.pytest_cache/
node_modules/
.venv/
venv/
# `terraform init` writes provider plugins to `.terraform/`, about 436M on a tree
# that has run the installer, and an apply writes state files that can hold
# secrets. Docker does not read `.gitignore`, and its patterns need `**/` to
# reach a subdirectory.
**/.terraform/
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
# An install also writes its variables (`terraform.tfvars`, through a `.tmp`
# file that an interrupted run can leave) and override files, which name the
# project, the cluster and the state bucket and can hold secrets.
**/*.tfvars
!**/*.tfvars.example
**/*.tfvars.json
**/*.tfvars.tmp
**/*_override.tf
**/*_override.tf.json
**/override.tf
**/override.tf.json

# Local configuration files (except tracked default .env)
.env
.env.*
!agents/shared/defaults/.env
**/vars.sh
# The hand-authored install configuration. It holds credentials, and the
# patterns above do not reach it: they anchor on a leading dot.
install.env
**/install.env
